## 1. Epistemic status of audit agreement

The report labels claims “triply supported,” “supported by two audits,” and “single-audit contribution.” This is useful for tracking convergence among reviewers, but it is not evidence that a scientific claim is true.

### Valid use

- prioritizing issues for review;
- identifying independent convergence;
- documenting disagreement;
- deciding which claims need external verification first.

### Invalid use

- treating three agreeing audits as proof;
- upgrading a conjecture to a theorem or empirical regularity;
- calling a thermodynamic or scaling claim settled because multiple language-model audits repeated it.

Every claim still requires the verifier appropriate to its type.

