## 7. Informational, political, and distributive content

The report’s expanded institutional requirements are valid as a checklist. Multi-agent incentives, asymmetric power, enforcement, and commons dynamics require explicit models. A single coordination variable \(\Theta_{coordination}\) is only a possible reduced representation; it is not established as a general state variable.

The “colonial metabolic pattern” identifies an important relational and distributive failure mode, but its operationalization requires explicit populations, flows, authority, burdens, and normative premises. It should not appear as a theorem without such specification.

